# Embedded Codex Agent Instructions

## Purpose And Reading Model

- This `codex/` tree is the embedded operating memory for `UnrealMCP5_6_1`. The repository root `AGENTS.md` is the critical adapter and remains binding.
- This repository is self-contained for routine agent, workflow, policy, MCP, and verification decisions. Parent workspace instructions, sibling repositories, submodules, and external `CubelessOps` are not active authority unless the user explicitly names that scope.
- Read the minimal bootstrap first: root `AGENTS.md`, this file, and `projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`. Then use progressive disclosure; do not load every linked document.
- Do not preload domain documents. Open a row in `docs/workflows/component-reading-router.md` only when the current request will actually inspect, edit, or verify that component; one row never imports unrelated rows.
- Resolve conflicts by instruction priority: system/developer and active runtime constraints, then explicit user instructions, then repository instructions. Within repository instructions, use the designated canonical policy for that subject; role files and handoff text cannot override it. Apply compatible additional safety conditions together, but do not use "the stricter rule wins" to revive conflicting or superseded guidance.
- Continue authorized work through completion using reasonable assumptions for routine choices. Approval already granted for the same task remains valid within its scope; follow `docs/policies/approvals.md`. If an instruction requires stopping, cite the exact file and clause, explain the concrete blocker, and continue independent authorized work where possible.
- Prefer the local-work permission profile in `docs/policies/local-permission-profile.md`. If runtime permissions are more restrictive, report that before broad project or MCP work; never work around active approval or safety boundaries.
- Broad runtime access never expands task scope or authorizes credential, secret, account, remote, destructive-history, unrelated-work, or system-security changes.

## Agent Work Visibility

- Keep the user informed in Korean. Use original spelling only for identifiers, paths, commands, APIs, exact errors, and literals where translation would reduce accuracy.
- Before meaningful work, state the active role, immediate objective, known target, and whether the step is inspection, mutation, verification, Git, or handoff.
- Before file, asset, editor, build, bridge, Git, or external-state mutation, briefly state what will change or run and why.
- During longer work, report concise milestones rather than per-command noise. When blocked, provide the blocker, evidence, and next safe option.
- Do not expose secrets, credentials, large logs, or low-signal command chatter.
- Honor an explicit request for silence or status-only behavior unless a safety, approval, destructive-action, or external-state notice is required. Role files may strengthen but not remove these duties.

## Text Encoding Safety

- Repository text uses UTF-8 as defined by `.editorconfig`. Preserve valid BOM and line-ending choices unless the task explicitly normalizes them.
- In Windows PowerShell 5.1, always read repository text with `Get-Content -Encoding UTF8`. Never rewrite a source from garbled terminal rendering.
- Use `apply_patch` for normal edits. If a script must write text, select an explicit UTF-8 encoder; for UTF-8 without BOM use `System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)` rather than Windows PowerShell 5.1 `Set-Content -Encoding UTF8`.
- If output looks corrupted, re-read with explicit UTF-8 and verify original bytes or `git diff` before editing.
- For a full audit, run `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File codex/scripts/check-text-encoding.ps1 -AllTracked`. The versioned pre-commit hook checks staged text automatically only in clones configured with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.

## Conditional Reading Index

- Workspace or executable paths: `docs/policies/workspace-portability.md`.
- Runtime/session/ACL permissions: `docs/policies/local-permission-profile.md`.
- Staging, commit, push, or multi-repository state: `docs/policies/git-repositories.md` and, when approval scope matters, `docs/policies/approvals.md`.
- Durable memory: `docs/policies/documentation-memory.md` only when the request touches it.
- Agent/model choice, verification cadence, or billable/API routes: `docs/policies/cost-control.md`.
- Cross-cutting mutation, C++, dependency, dirty-work, editor-lifecycle, UTF-8, or destructive risk: use `docs/policies/safety-matrix.md` to load the canonical source before acting.
- Repository-owned Codex skill creation, review, or installation: inspect `skills/` and follow the applicable `SKILL.md`; keep Claude adapter material in its separate integration tree.
- Component implementation and verification: read only the matching row in `docs/workflows/component-reading-router.md` when that component is actually in scope.
- Saved Unreal content or project API changes: `docs/policies/authoring-dependency-boundary.md`.
- Non-UnrealMCP project C++: `docs/policies/project-cpp-approval-gate.md` before mutation.
- Named roles: the matching file under `agents/`.
- RPC/transport reliability: `docs/workflows/mcp-rpc-verification-first.md`.
- Smoke validation: `agents/tivret-mcp.md` and `docs/workflows/mcp-smoke-test-protocol.md`.
- Upstream update: `agents/mcp-upstream-manager.md` and `docs/workflows/mcp-upstream-update.md`.
- Release verification: `agents/mcp-release-verifier.md` and the project binding verification entry point.
- Claude adapter work: `integrations/claude-code/README.md`. Keep Claude wrappers and manifests outside the Codex `skills/` tree.
- New section bootstrap, cross-repository orchestration, or rule promotion: the matching workflow under `docs/workflows/`.
- Agent-instruction or routing evaluation: `docs/workflows/agent-instruction-evaluation.md`.
- Do not load external project bindings unless the user explicitly names that external repository.

## Workspace, Git, And Concurrency

- Discover the active repository root; do not assume a fixed drive. Resolve executable paths from the repository, active `.uproject`, or a documented explicit environment variable.
- Do not inspect or resolve external repositories during routine work. If an explicitly requested external workspace is missing, report its name rather than guessing another drive.
- `codex/` and `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP` belong to this repository. Never stage unrelated dirty work.
- Before substantial edits, check status and recent history. Treat unfamiliar changes as another agent's work and respect current user-stated domain locks.
- Before pushing an existing tracked branch, pull with `--ff-only` and merge shared documents additively. Follow `docs/policies/git-repositories.md` for a new untracked branch and the complete boundary.
- Treat the effective configured UE editor bridge endpoint as shared; the project default is `127.0.0.1:55561`. Editor launch, close, map changes, dirty prompts, and `QUIT_EDITOR` affect every connected agent, so check process and log context first.
- Historical logs may retain absolute paths as evidence, but executable defaults must remain portable.

## Safety Sources Of Truth

- The root `AGENTS.md` retains the exact UTF-8, repository scope, unfamiliar-dirty-work, `c++1218`, UnrealMCP-plugin-exception, and finished-content-independence tripwires.
- `docs/policies/safety-matrix.md` routes risk signals to canonical sources; it is not a replacement rule body.
- `docs/policies/authoring-dependency-boundary.md` is the detailed source for pre-mutation and pre-promotion dependency checks.
- `docs/policies/project-cpp-approval-gate.md` is the detailed source for project C++ scope, valid approval forms, the UnrealMCP exception, and gate commands.
- A historical non-MCP implementation never becomes standing approval for later source edits.

## Execution Economy

- Follow `docs/policies/cost-control.md` for the canonical model, subagent, second-eye, verification-tier, evidence-reuse, and release/torture rules.
- Simple answers, status checks, routine inspection, and single-file low-risk edits stay with one default agent. Cost never overrides a safety source, required review, or promotion gate.

## Durable Memory

- Keep reusable operating rules in Git-tracked Markdown when documentation is part of the current approved scope; do not rely on chat or agent-private storage as the only canonical copy.
- Store project-specific paths, systems, and exceptions in the project index or matching project documents rather than expanding the bootstrap.
- Push durable documentation only when the user has authorized push for that repository and branch in the same task, following `docs/policies/approvals.md`.
- Before replacing a large instruction adapter with a thin form, preserve the previous source in `snapshots/` and reference it from the new adapter. Historical snapshots are immutable.
